## EARS Requirement

When the user invokes the \`graph\` subcommand with a node ID, the system shall display the node's relationships (parents, children, related nodes) from the knowledge DAG stored in INDEX.json.

## Test by Contract (DbC)

### Preconditions
- INDEX.json exists with a valid \`graph\` object
- Graph contains \`nodes\`, \`edges\`, and \`reachability\` data
- Node ID argument is provided (document ID or chunk ID)

### Postconditions
- Displays node title and type (Document or Chunk)
- Lists all incoming edges (what points TO this node)
- Lists all outgoing edges (what this node points TO)
- Shows edge types (Parent, Sequential, Related) with weights
- Displays reachable nodes count if available

### Invariants
- Non-existent node ID returns "Node not found: {id}"
- Edge weights are displayed with 2 decimal precision
- Output format is consistent regardless of node type

